WEBVTT

00:04.480 --> 00:06.430
Meow, meow!

00:07.320 --> 00:08.980
Come on out!

00:09.910 --> 00:11.970
Here, kitty!

00:34.850 --> 00:36.240
Oh, just end me now!

00:36.240 --> 00:37.480
Kasahara-san?

00:40.560 --> 00:42.130
Kasahara-san...

00:42.400 --> 00:45.090
You really love cats, huh?

00:45.090 --> 00:47.740
I bet you think it's weird that I do!

00:47.740 --> 00:49.590
N-No, I don't!

00:49.590 --> 00:51.320
Oh, for crying out loud!

00:51.320 --> 00:54.650
Why did <i>you</i> have to see me doing 
something so embarrassing?!

00:54.650 --> 00:58.180
I-I don't really think it's embarrassing.

00:58.180 --> 00:59.820
I found it endearing.

00:59.820 --> 01:02.890
That meow? Meow...

01:02.890 --> 01:04.940
Wait, are you making fun of me?

01:04.940 --> 01:05.670
What?!

01:06.080 --> 01:08.350
I-I swear I'm not.

01:08.350 --> 01:10.340
It really was cute!

01:11.990 --> 01:13.580
Nishimura-san...

01:14.150 --> 01:15.850
You have a cat, right?

01:15.850 --> 01:18.200
Huh? Yeah.

01:18.200 --> 01:19.340
Let me...

01:21.380 --> 01:23.480
Let me meet him some time.

01:24.880 --> 01:26.490
S-Sure!

01:26.720 --> 01:28.550
Well, see you tomorrow!

01:30.930 --> 01:31.810
Huh?

01:32.470 --> 01:33.560
She's fast...

03:00.860 --> 03:04.950
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

03:05.910 --> 03:11.750
<i>Episode 11 "The Swift Reaper Alliance, the Cursed Song, and Christmas"</i>

03:20.410 --> 03:21.670
<i>A leaf...</i>

03:23.220 --> 03:24.760
Nishimura-san!

03:25.420 --> 03:28.090
Great job watering the flower beds!

03:28.790 --> 03:31.910
Say, say! Could I water them next time, too?

03:31.110 --> 03:32.550
<i>Notice already.</i>

03:31.910 --> 03:32.550
Sure.

03:32.770 --> 03:33.790
Yay!

03:33.790 --> 03:37.460
That means more time to talk with you!

03:37.460 --> 03:39.080
<i>Oh, come on!</i>

03:37.910 --> 03:39.770
I'll help out starting tomorrow!

03:39.770 --> 03:40.820
O-Okay.

03:40.820 --> 03:42.290
I can't wait!

03:42.290 --> 03:43.280
Hold it!

03:42.290 --> 03:43.490
Oh, Nishimura-san!

03:43.490 --> 03:44.080
Huh?

03:47.130 --> 03:48.280
This was in your hair.

03:48.640 --> 03:49.360
Ah...

03:50.570 --> 03:52.180
Thanks.

03:52.180 --> 03:53.020
Sure.

03:53.540 --> 03:55.290
That's not fair, Kasahara-san!

03:55.290 --> 03:56.310
In what way?!

03:56.310 --> 03:59.820
When did you somehow get closer
to Nishimura-san than me?

03:59.820 --> 04:01.720
What?! I have not!

04:01.720 --> 04:04.040
Huh? You haven't...?

04:06.510 --> 04:09.990
Th-This is totally normal.

04:09.990 --> 04:11.250
What?!

04:11.250 --> 04:12.720
This is just normal?!

04:13.000 --> 04:15.840
So that means you could get even <i>closer</i>!

04:15.840 --> 04:16.880
What?!

04:16.880 --> 04:18.550
Talk about positive thinking!

04:19.790 --> 04:21.110
Thanks!

04:21.110 --> 04:22.730
No, that wasn't a compliment.

04:23.330 --> 04:24.160
Huh?

04:24.660 --> 04:30.570
I mean, Kasahara the Swift and 
Nishimura the Grim Reaper are hanging out.

04:31.640 --> 04:34.820
That's so cool!
You're the Swift Reaper Alliance!

04:35.780 --> 04:38.630
W-We're just normal friends!

04:40.420 --> 04:42.550
F-Friends...

04:42.880 --> 04:44.720
The strongest duo!

04:44.720 --> 04:46.380
Enough with the nickname stuff!

04:46.380 --> 04:48.570
But yours are so awesome!

04:48.570 --> 04:50.400
No, they're not!

04:56.340 --> 04:57.240
Okay!

04:57.600 --> 05:00.110
<b>That-There Station</b>

05:00.110 --> 05:02.860
<b>Let's go to That-There Zoo!</b>

05:00.110 --> 05:02.860
<b>That-There Railway</b>

05:11.280 --> 05:14.000
G-Good morning, Takada-kun.

05:14.000 --> 05:15.390
Good morning!

05:15.390 --> 05:17.540
You're real dressed up today!

05:18.080 --> 05:21.160
I-I figured I should for a trip like this.

05:21.160 --> 05:23.000
D-Does it look weird?

05:23.000 --> 05:24.420
It's not weird!

05:24.420 --> 05:25.870
You look really nice in that!

05:25.870 --> 05:28.260
Huh? Th-Thanks.

05:29.010 --> 05:30.990
We're just waiting on Hino-kun now.

05:30.990 --> 05:31.740
Yep.

05:32.810 --> 05:36.120
<i>He's always the one complimenting me.</i>

05:36.480 --> 05:40.320
<i>I want to make Takada-kun happy, too.</i>

05:40.780 --> 05:44.000
<i>Today's the day I compliment Takada-kun!</i>

05:44.710 --> 05:47.070
Y-You're also...

05:48.970 --> 05:52.980
You're also really cool today!

05:53.270 --> 05:55.050
Huh? How exactly?

05:58.650 --> 06:00.700
<i>How exactly?!</i>

06:01.180 --> 06:03.120
<i>H-His personality?</i>

06:03.440 --> 06:07.270
<i>But that makes it sound 
like he doesn't </i>look<i> cool.</i>

06:07.270 --> 06:11.010
<i>Ah, but it'd be so embarrassing to say, 
"Everything about you is cool!"</i>

06:12.400 --> 06:14.440
Everything about you is cool...

06:14.810 --> 06:15.970
<i>I said it!</i>

06:16.790 --> 06:18.760
Thanks, Nishimura-san!

06:18.760 --> 06:19.460
Huh?

06:19.760 --> 06:23.730
I think your curse power is super cool, too!

06:23.730 --> 06:25.800
Way, way cooler than me!

06:25.800 --> 06:29.780
That's why I can never
 stop thinking about you!

06:35.850 --> 06:39.330
<i>I wanted to be the one 
making Takada-kun happy!</i>

06:42.470 --> 06:44.510
I wonder where Hino-kun is...

06:53.680 --> 06:57.770
<i>C-Complimenting people is hard.</i>

07:07.270 --> 07:08.680
My bad!

07:09.880 --> 07:11.500
I ended up running late!

07:11.980 --> 07:15.300
My arms just can't get 
used to this jacket...

07:16.380 --> 07:18.280
What's the matter, Takada?

07:18.280 --> 07:19.680
You've got a grin on your face.

07:19.680 --> 07:20.310
Huh?

07:22.260 --> 07:23.830
I wonder why.

07:25.670 --> 07:28.670
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

07:25.670 --> 07:28.670
<b>That-There Zoo</b>

07:25.670 --> 07:28.670
Free Admission
for Grade Schoolers

07:30.910 --> 07:32.000
Hey!

07:32.000 --> 07:35.300
I saw you on Sunday on that 
TV special about ghosts!

07:37.810 --> 07:41.440
That ghost woman sure was creepy.

07:43.040 --> 07:45.490
Th-That wasn't me...

07:45.490 --> 07:48.080
You mean that live broadcast, right?

07:48.670 --> 07:52.220
In that case, I don't think that 
ghost could have been Nishimura-san.

07:52.700 --> 07:53.950
Why not?

07:54.290 --> 08:00.640
Because Nishimura-san was out with 
me <i>all</i> Sunday long, isn't that right?

08:00.640 --> 08:02.460
Y-Yeah.

08:03.560 --> 08:05.270
<i>That's a date!</i>

08:05.830 --> 08:06.730
That's a date!

08:06.730 --> 08:07.410
Huh?

08:07.410 --> 08:10.500
No way, no how. We're still kids.

08:10.500 --> 08:12.370
We just met up at the station...

08:12.370 --> 08:13.550
That's a date!

08:13.880 --> 08:15.850
And went to the zoo together!

08:16.240 --> 08:17.580
That's called a date!

08:17.780 --> 08:20.290
Nishimura-san was so cute all dressed up!

08:20.290 --> 08:21.710
That's absolutely a date!

08:21.710 --> 08:23.690
I-I wouldn't call it...

08:23.690 --> 08:25.020
No, it was a date!

08:25.020 --> 08:26.270
Your face says it was!

08:26.590 --> 08:28.830
But Hino-kun was there, too.

08:30.630 --> 08:33.560
Th-That's not a date...

08:34.310 --> 08:36.420
<i>Safe!</i>

08:37.580 --> 08:39.930
I left pretty quick, though.

08:39.930 --> 08:42.290
I had plans with Umi.

08:42.290 --> 08:44.730
You went on a date, too?!

08:45.540 --> 08:48.540
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

08:48.540 --> 08:51.920
Shopping List

<u>Cheaper at Shimizu Supermarket</u>
Scallions 1 bunch
Eggs 1 carton
<u>Cheaper at Osamu Grocer</u>
Napa cabbage 1 head
Shirataki noodles 1 pack

We're having hot pot tonight!!
Thanks,
Dad

08:51.930 --> 08:54.340
Scallion, scallion, eggs...

08:56.830 --> 08:58.170
What song is that?

09:02.370 --> 09:05.390
T-T-T-T-Takada-kun!

09:06.040 --> 09:07.850
H-How long have you been there?

09:07.850 --> 09:10.580
Huh? Since we were outside the park.

09:11.360 --> 09:13.190
<i>That was a while ago!</i>

09:13.510 --> 09:15.620
What was that song just now?

09:16.150 --> 09:18.740
D-Don't ask, Takada-kun!

09:18.740 --> 09:20.380
Huh? Why not?

09:20.610 --> 09:22.350
W-Well...

09:22.880 --> 09:25.950
<i>I was just singing to myself 
without thinking...</i>

09:27.260 --> 09:28.630
Don't tell me...

09:29.660 --> 09:31.220
Was it a cursed song?!

09:32.600 --> 09:33.390
Huh?

09:34.330 --> 09:36.360
Kitagawa-kun told me about it!

09:36.360 --> 09:39.420
He said your songs are cursed songs!

09:39.780 --> 09:42.100
O-Oh, did he?

09:42.100 --> 09:43.970
What an awful thing to say...

09:43.970 --> 09:47.260
Cursed songs are pretty adorable, huh?

09:48.890 --> 09:52.350
Hey, hey! Let me hear more
of that cursed song!

09:55.840 --> 09:59.300
Wh-Why do you want to hear it so badly?

09:59.300 --> 10:04.370
What? Because cursed songs sound so awesome!

10:04.370 --> 10:06.940
Although it was cuter than I imagined.

10:08.700 --> 10:11.080
Oh, want me to hold your bag?

10:11.460 --> 10:15.230
D-Doing that still won't make me sing.

10:21.530 --> 10:23.890
<i>He looks so disappointed.</i>

10:27.290 --> 10:30.630
<i>Cursed songs are pretty adorable, huh?</i>

10:48.100 --> 10:50.700
Scallion, scallion, eggs...

10:54.880 --> 10:57.050
Da da da, let's go...

10:55.630 --> 11:06.120
<b>That-There Shopping District</b>

10:56.120 --> 10:57.310
I knew it!

10:57.310 --> 10:59.810
The cursed song is way cuter than I thought!

10:59.810 --> 11:00.970
Why is that?!

11:00.970 --> 11:02.260
B-Beats me...

11:02.260 --> 11:03.730
What comes after that?!

11:03.730 --> 11:05.270
Huh? Nothing!

11:06.930 --> 11:11.940
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

11:17.990 --> 11:20.120
Hey, Takada-kun!

11:20.860 --> 11:24.160
Have you ever heard of 
"illicit fraternization"?

11:24.160 --> 11:25.360
What's that?

11:25.600 --> 11:29.560
It's a very naughty thing 
that troublemakers do.

11:29.560 --> 11:32.870
Takada-kun, you're doing it
without realizing it.

11:32.870 --> 11:35.720
What?! R-Really?!

11:35.720 --> 11:39.180
You know, you're so close 
with Nishimura-san...

11:39.180 --> 11:44.440
B-Being close with Nishimura-san 
counts as "illicit fractalization"?

11:46.650 --> 11:49.420
Fraternization, not fractalization.

11:49.420 --> 11:50.460
And it sure does!

11:51.050 --> 11:56.890
Nowadays, chatting up the opposite sex 
willy-nilly counts as illicit fraternization.

11:57.240 --> 12:00.100
Are you sure you should be 
so close with Nishimura-san?

12:00.100 --> 12:03.750
At this rate, both of you will 
be branded troublemakers.

12:03.750 --> 12:04.950
Oh, no!

12:04.950 --> 12:05.900
That's scary!

12:06.200 --> 12:07.880
We'd be troublemakers...

12:07.880 --> 12:09.910
You girls would be, too, right?

12:12.910 --> 12:14.870
H-How do you figure?!

12:14.870 --> 12:19.420
W-Well, you're girls, 
but you talk to me all the time.

12:19.420 --> 12:23.410
That counts as, uh...
illicit fraternization, right?

12:24.210 --> 12:28.290
All of you and Nishimura-san are 
troublemakers because of me...

12:28.290 --> 12:30.070
I-I'm so sorry!

12:31.930 --> 12:34.330
Wh-Why are <i>you</i> apologizing?!

12:34.330 --> 12:35.880
<i>He's way too pure!</i>

12:38.240 --> 12:40.560
I-It's okay, Takada-kun.

12:41.390 --> 12:46.380
Just talking to girls doesn't count as illicit
fraternization or make you a troublemaker.

12:46.380 --> 12:47.820
What? Really?

12:49.560 --> 12:51.310
What a relief.

12:51.310 --> 12:55.580
If I couldn't talk to you, 
I'd be so lonely I'd die!

12:55.830 --> 12:57.150
I'm safe!

13:02.370 --> 13:04.450
M-Me, too...

13:10.270 --> 13:11.180
Man...

13:11.580 --> 13:14.350
Alone with an upperclassman 
on Christmas Eve?

13:15.470 --> 13:18.470
Just you two library officers?

13:19.120 --> 13:21.850
C-C'mon, Yuki-chan.

13:21.850 --> 13:23.900
Stop teasing me.

13:24.240 --> 13:26.580
Does he even read books?

13:26.580 --> 13:30.110
Surprisingly, he reads way more than I do.

13:30.950 --> 13:33.700
More than Kasumi the bookworm?

13:33.700 --> 13:36.300
You really can't judge a book by its cover.

13:37.250 --> 13:41.260
He acts so mature that I 
can't help but be nervous...

13:41.820 --> 13:45.070
Hey, my outfit isn't weird, is it?

13:45.070 --> 13:46.760
Is it too plain?

13:46.760 --> 13:48.680
It's fine, it's fine.

13:48.680 --> 13:50.330
It's a very "you" outfit.

13:51.580 --> 13:53.760
Ah! Kasumi-oneechan!

13:54.140 --> 13:56.780
Hey! I came to visit, Taiyou-kun.

13:57.040 --> 13:58.280
Listen to this, Taiyou!

13:58.280 --> 14:02.420
Kasumi's got a Christmas date today 
with an older middle schooler!

14:02.420 --> 14:05.400
What?! A Christmas date?!

14:05.400 --> 14:07.840
Awesome! That's amazing!

14:07.840 --> 14:11.770
C'mon, cut it out, Yuki-chan! Taiyou-kun!

14:12.160 --> 14:13.670
What about you?

14:15.000 --> 14:18.460
I need to pay my duties at a 
little place called cram school!

14:18.460 --> 14:20.850
That's amazing in its own way!

14:21.160 --> 14:23.690
It's nice that kids are so honest.

14:24.140 --> 14:26.510
I need to be more honest with myself.

14:27.130 --> 14:29.130
I'll do my best, Taiyou-kun!

14:30.650 --> 14:32.700
Yeah, you can do it!

14:32.700 --> 14:35.120
Wait, aren't you headed out, too?

14:35.960 --> 14:38.100
Oh yeah, that's right!

14:38.570 --> 14:41.650
I'm going shopping with Nishimura-san!

14:45.770 --> 14:46.990
There.

14:51.370 --> 14:53.570
<i>Today is Christmas Eve.</i>

14:53.820 --> 14:58.920
<i>We decided to hold a party 
at Takada-kun's with everyone.</i>

14:59.240 --> 15:02.010
<i>I'm really looking forward to it.</i>

15:03.520 --> 15:05.940
Ah! Nishimura-san!

15:11.680 --> 15:13.190
Yay!

15:13.190 --> 15:16.040
Christmas party at the Takada household!

15:16.040 --> 15:17.700
It's almost time!

15:17.700 --> 15:21.020
Y-You do know we're going shopping, right?

15:21.340 --> 15:24.620
You should know better, Nishimura-san.

15:24.620 --> 15:28.270
Preparing is the most fun
part of these things!

15:28.960 --> 15:30.450
I-I see.

15:31.530 --> 15:35.580
I had this marked on my 
calendar a whole month ago!

15:35.580 --> 15:37.290
That's amazing.

15:37.580 --> 15:42.360
As for me, it's my first time 
spending Christmas with friends.

15:42.360 --> 15:44.180
So I'm not sure what to do...

15:44.500 --> 15:48.920
Christmas is a time it's okay to indulge
in things you wouldn't normally!

15:49.190 --> 15:51.620
Um, like what?

15:52.300 --> 15:55.360
Nishimura-san, have you 
heard of sparkling cider?

15:55.360 --> 15:56.520
Nope.

15:56.520 --> 15:58.610
It's juice that looks like alcohol!

15:59.220 --> 16:00.850
Even kids can drink it!

16:00.850 --> 16:04.450
When you raise a glass of it,
 you feel like a grown-up!

16:04.450 --> 16:05.890
Huh.

16:06.170 --> 16:09.910
I wouldn't be surprised if Hino-kun 
actually gets tipsy drinking it!

16:09.910 --> 16:11.560
Even though it's just juice?

16:11.560 --> 16:14.650
Also, we can have cake and fried chicken!

16:14.960 --> 16:16.680
And then there's...

16:16.680 --> 16:18.260
Exchanging gifts!

16:18.260 --> 16:19.920
I'm real excited for that!

16:19.920 --> 16:21.880
Exchanging gifts?

16:21.880 --> 16:24.670
Yeah, I came prepared!

16:25.090 --> 16:28.540
Look forward to my present, Nishimura-san!

16:29.700 --> 16:33.180
A-Are you sure you want 
to raise expectations like that?

16:33.180 --> 16:35.370
It's A-okay!

16:35.370 --> 16:38.410
After all, it's Christmas!

16:39.180 --> 16:41.310
<i>Takada-kun looks like he's having fun.</i>

16:39.360 --> 16:41.030
Christmas!

16:41.030 --> 16:43.930
I hope Santa comes!

16:42.070 --> 16:45.110
<i>It's giving me butterflies, as well.</i>

16:50.110 --> 16:52.200
It's from your house.

16:52.200 --> 16:55.460
Oh, Hino-kun must have gotten there first!

16:55.460 --> 16:56.750
I'll answer it.

16:56.750 --> 16:58.910
Right now, we're pretending 
to be signal troops!

16:58.910 --> 17:00.320
S-Sure.

17:00.520 --> 17:03.170
Come in! This is the decoration squad.

17:03.170 --> 17:07.530
Decoration campaign is progressing smoothly 
thanks to valiant efforts from Private Umi!

17:07.530 --> 17:08.460
Over!

17:08.990 --> 17:10.910
You help, too, Dai-chan!

17:12.460 --> 17:13.830
Copy that!

17:13.830 --> 17:16.520
Keep up the good work!

17:16.520 --> 17:19.380
The shopping squad is about to secure snacks!

17:19.380 --> 17:20.410
Over!

17:20.410 --> 17:21.650
<i>This seems fun.</i>

17:22.210 --> 17:23.340
Roger!

17:23.340 --> 17:25.690
I'll relay the message to Private Nishimura!

17:25.690 --> 17:26.940
End transmission!

17:27.970 --> 17:30.570
He said they heard back from Kasahara-san.

17:30.570 --> 17:32.340
She's coming, but she'll be late.

17:33.290 --> 17:34.970
I-I see!

17:35.910 --> 17:38.370
<i>I'm glad I made up my mind and invited her.</i>

17:40.460 --> 17:42.490
Hey, hey, Nishimura-san.

17:42.490 --> 17:44.680
Where was the pastry shop again?

17:44.680 --> 17:47.490
Um... let me check.

17:50.790 --> 17:53.350
Th-That way, maybe?

17:53.350 --> 17:55.470
Okay! Off we go!

17:56.930 --> 17:59.430
Oh, not that way, Takada-kun!

18:00.390 --> 18:01.920
Huh? Which way?

18:02.420 --> 18:03.730
That way?

18:03.730 --> 18:05.150
Hey, look over there.

18:06.190 --> 18:09.710
You think those kids are 
also on a Christmas date?

18:09.710 --> 18:10.630
Maybe.

18:11.150 --> 18:12.610
How adorable!

18:13.860 --> 18:16.490
A Ch-Christmas date...

18:16.490 --> 18:18.590
A Christmas date?

18:18.590 --> 18:20.650
I see, so this is...

18:27.330 --> 18:30.370
The two of us feel a little 
more grown-up today!

18:30.370 --> 18:32.200
We'll be drinking sparkling cider, too!

18:34.270 --> 18:36.290
Y-Yeah.

18:36.920 --> 18:38.610
Okay, let's go!

18:40.870 --> 18:45.110
<i>It looks like Takada-kun 
doesn't really get it.</i>

18:46.040 --> 18:48.400
<i>In a way, that's a relief.</i>

18:50.420 --> 18:51.210
Ah!

18:52.620 --> 18:54.300
It's Kasumi-chan!

18:54.300 --> 18:55.750
Kasumi-chan?

18:55.980 --> 18:58.400
Yeah! Kasumi-oneechan.

18:58.400 --> 19:00.460
She's my sister's friend.

19:00.790 --> 19:02.810
She always comes over to play!

19:02.810 --> 19:05.450
She's really good at video games!

19:05.660 --> 19:06.860
Huh...

19:07.520 --> 19:10.290
Ah, she's with a boy.

19:10.770 --> 19:15.410
I heard from my sister that Kasumi-oneechan
 was going on a Christmas date.

19:15.660 --> 19:18.870
Just like us! All lovey-dovey!

19:21.220 --> 19:23.210
N-No way...

19:23.610 --> 19:26.540
But what are they doing at the park?

19:26.540 --> 19:28.070
It's so cold out.

19:28.070 --> 19:30.730
Why don't they play video 
games or something?

19:30.730 --> 19:32.450
While drinking sparkling cider!

19:33.000 --> 19:35.070
You sure do like sparkling cider.

19:35.690 --> 19:37.400
I should call out to them.

19:37.400 --> 19:37.920
What?!

19:37.920 --> 19:40.310
Y-You shouldn't interrupt their date!

19:40.310 --> 19:41.970
It's fine, it's fine!

19:41.970 --> 19:44.160
Kasumi-oneechan's nice!

19:51.290 --> 19:53.610
Hey...

20:39.350 --> 20:40.630
<i>What's wrong?</i>

20:41.930 --> 20:43.530
<i>Nishimura-san...</i>

20:43.530 --> 20:46.200
<i>When we grow up, can I kiss you?</i>

20:55.830 --> 20:57.770
Th-The cake...

20:58.890 --> 20:59.680
Huh?

21:00.310 --> 21:03.400
We need to go buy the cake.

21:04.490 --> 21:05.660
Y-Yeah.

21:07.280 --> 21:08.780
That's right.

21:11.790 --> 21:16.750
<b>X-mas Sale</b>

21:14.600 --> 21:16.110
<i>I wonder what it is.</i>

21:16.760 --> 21:19.130
<i>We always hold hands...</i>

21:20.000 --> 21:23.790
<i>But today, it feels a little warmer.</i>

23:13.280 --> 23:14.910
Yo!

23:14.910 --> 23:17.200
Thanks for doing the shopping!

23:17.200 --> 23:19.340
You two must be cold.

23:19.340 --> 23:20.910
Hurry on inside.

23:21.140 --> 23:23.610
H-Hey there.

23:26.820 --> 23:28.940
<i>Huh? Wh-What gives?</i>

23:28.940 --> 23:31.460
<i>Did something happen with these two?!</i>

23:34.930 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next time...</b>

23:34.930 --> 23:39.930
<b>The Christmas Party Confession</b>
